<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick III, Elector Palatine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1515">1515</a>–<a href="/years/1576">1576</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Frederick the Pious</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick III, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elector-palatine">Elector Palatine</a>, called the Pious, came from the Palatinate-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simmern">Simmern</a> line and became elector in 1559. He made the Palatinate the first Calvinist state of the Empire and sponsored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg-catechism">Heidelberg Catechism</a> of 1563. He supported Protestants in the French and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> wars of religion, making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a> a centre of Reformed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestantism">Protestantism</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-elector-palatine.jpg" alt="Frederick III, Elector Palatine" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_der_Fromme.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
